    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Built in 2001 as part of a private development of just 9 houses in a secluded little cul-de-sac close to the shop, creche and primary school in Mountshannon, this house stands on a small site measuring 600 square metres.  The house itself extends to 101 square metres, 1091 square feet, and has a very manageable back garden with a stream running at the rear.  It has its own parking space and there is additional off street parking in the common area at the front.\r\n\r\nThe house has three bedrooms all on the first floor and is connected to all mains services including high speed broadband.  Oil fired central heating is installed and there is a solid fuel stove in the sitting room.  All windows are made of wood and are double glazed.  Building Energy Rating is C.\r\n\r\nGround floor accommodation extends to an entrance porch, a central hallway, a kitchen / dining room, a sitting room and a W/C.  On the first floor are the main bathroom with bath and shower and the three bedrooms one of which has a shower room ensuite.  There is a folding attic stairs leading to a fully floored out attic which gives plenty of accessible storage space.  When the house was built, foundations were laid for a rear extension which gives further options to prospective buyers.\r\n\r\nROOM DIMENSIONS\r\nEntrance Porch\r\n1.2m x 1.9m Tiled floor\r\n\r\nHallway\r\n3.9m x 1.7m\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining\r\n3.0m x 5.8m Wood and tiled floor\r\n\r\nSitting Room\r\n3.0m x 5.8m Wood floor, Solid fuel stove\r\n\r\nGround floor W.C.\r\n1.7m x 1.7m Tiled\r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\n3.7m x 3.0m Laminate floor, Built in wardrobes, En suite measures 3.0m x 1.5m with electric shower\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\r\n3.4m x 2.7m Laminate floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\n2.9m x 2.1m Laminate floor\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\n2.4m x 2.0m Power shower\r\n\r\nLanding\r\n1.8m x 3.2m Laminate wood floor\r\n\r\nThe house has been rented for many years and will need some freshening up but its location in such a nice quiet residential development is likely to make it very sought after.\r\n\r\nViewings are by appointment only with the sole agents.  Phone Noel Hogan today on 087 2651377 to organise your viewing!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Connected to all mains services including high speed broadband  \r\n\r\nOil fired central heating is installed and there is a solid fuel stove in the sitting room  \r\n\r\nAll windows are made of wood and are double glazed\r\n\r\nFoundations were laid for a rear extension which gives further options to prospective buyers\r\n\r\nGreat location near shop, creche, school and church\r\n\r\nLocallink return bus 4 times daily to Ennis\r\n\r\n45 minutes drive to Ennis, Limerick and Shannon. One hour drive to Galway city.\r\n\r\nRented for many years property will need freshening up but its location in a nice quiet residential development is likely to make it very sought after"
      },
